    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Endpoint">Endpoint</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_ApiKey">API key</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_ApiKeyHelp">Paste it here only if the provider requires it. For local LM Studio and Ollama this is usually empty. Do not paste your ChatGPT key here: it must be an API key from the selected provider.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Model">Model</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TestProvider">Test provider</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_UseLmStudioFree">Use LM Studio free</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_UseOllamaFree">Use Ollama free</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_FreeLocalFallback">Free local fallback</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_LocalFallbackCheckbox">If the cloud provider fails because of quota, limits or high demand, try local providers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_LocalFallbackHelp">To make this work, LM Studio must have its local server enabled or Ollama must be running with the model downloaded. The API key is empty for local providers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_OutputLanguage">Output language</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Tone">Tone</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Length">Length</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_LengthHelp">The global length also guides how many items are returned in lists. For text, length per token lets you tune each block: for synopsis, Short=1 paragraph, Medium=2, Long=3 and Extra long=4-5.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_LengthPerToken">Length per token</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_CurrentMetadata">Current metadata</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_CurrentMetadataHelp">Use as context lets the AI consider existing data without necessarily copying it. Normalize tries to fix and unify current metadata. Ignore does not send those details to the AI.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_StrictCompanyAgeRegion">Do not invent companies, age ratings or region unless reasonably sure</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_ExtraInstructions">Extra custom instructions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_ExtraInstructionsHelp">Use this for additional editorial rules: brand tone, words to avoid, desired structure, preferred names or criteria for deciding whether a detail is reliable.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_New">New</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Delete">Delete</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_RestoreDefaults">Restore defaults</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TemplateName">Template name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TemplateHtmlHelp">You can use HTML in the template. Playnite renders tags such as &amp;lt;p&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;h3&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;ul&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;li&amp;gt; and &amp;lt;br/&amp;gt;, so the description does not appear crammed together.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_DescriptionTokensTitle">Tokens available for the description</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Token">Token</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Reference">Reference</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_ImageSources">Image sources</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceKeysAndTests">Source keys and tests</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_OfficialSteam">Official Steam</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_OfficialSteamHelp">No API key required. Uses public Steam assets when the game can be matched to an AppID.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TestOfficialSteam">Test official Steam</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SteamGridDbHelp">Get it from your SteamGridDB profile, under Preferences/API. It is optional for Steam games, but recommended: it adds community covers, heroes/backgrounds and icons when official Steam does not have a suitable image.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_OpenSteamGridDb">Open SteamGridDB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TestSteamGridDb">Test SteamGridDB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_RawgHelp">RAWG requires an API key for each request. It mainly provides main images and screenshots for backgrounds.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TestRawg">Test RAWG</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_MobyGamesHelp">MobyGames uses api_key and can provide covers and screenshots, especially useful for classic games.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TestMobyGames">Test MobyGames</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_IgdbHelp">The plugin automatically generates the Twitch/IGDB Access Token with these details. You do not need to copy temporary tokens manually. Provides covers, screenshots and artworks.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TestIgdb">Test IGDB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Media">Media</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Field">Field</sys:String>
